font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 11,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.30.020 
Interference with parade or procession prohibited – exception.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A person shall not
interfere with a parade or procession.  A person shall not drive a vehicle that
is not part of a parade or procession between the vehicles of a parade or
procession.  This section does not apply at intersections where traffic is
controlled by traffic control devices unless a deputy is present at the
intersections to direct traffic so as to preserve the continuity of the parade
or procession.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 12,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;page-break-after:avoid'><a
name="_Toc519075539"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>14A.40         MOTORIZED
FOOT SCOOTERS</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.40.010   General
provisions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.40.020   Duties
of parents or guardians.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.40.030   Penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.40.010 
General provisions.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A.  A person operating
a motorized foot scooter shall ensure that the scooter is equipped with a brake
that enables the operator to make the braked wheels skid on dry, level, clean
pavement.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  A person
shall not use a motorized foot scooter at any time from one half hour before
sunset to one half hour after sunrise.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  A person
shall not operate a motorized foot scooter on county roads, alleys, county
recreational trails and park property unless the operator is at least thirteen
years old.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          D.  A person
operating a motorized foot scooter or riding as a passenger on a motorized foot
scooter upon any county road, alley, recreational trail or park property shall
comply with all laws related to the use of bicycle helmets, including wearing a
protective helmet designed for bicycle safety that meets or exceeds the safety
standards adopted by the United States Consumer Product Safety Commission or set
by the American National Standards Institute in effect on the effective date of
this ordinance, or such subsequent nationally recognized standard for bicycle
helmet performance as the county may adopt by ordinance.  The helmet must be
equipped with either a neck strap or chinstrap that shall be fastened securely
while the motorized foot scooter is in motion.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          E.  A person
operating a motorized foot scooter has the same rights and duties applicable to
bicycles when on a county road, except when traveling upon a crosswalk or in a
pedestrian zone, and shall follow the instructions of traffic control signals,
signs and other control devices applicable to vehicles and pedestrians, unless
otherwise directed by a deputy.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          F.  A person
shall not operate a motorized foot scooter on a sidewalk.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          G.  A person
shall not operate a motorized foot scooter on:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            1.  A
county road with a posted maximum speed limit greater than twenty-five miles
per hour; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>            2.  County
parks facilities, including parks, recreational trails, open space or other
property, under the jurisdiction of the parks and recreation division of the
department of natural resources and parks, unless the facility has been
specifically designated and posted for that use in accordance with K.C.C. chapter
7.12.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 14,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.40.020 
Duties of parents or guardians.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The parent of a child
or the guardian of a ward shall not authorize or knowingly permit the child or
ward to violate K.C.C. 14A.40.010.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 15,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>14A.40.030   Penalty.</b> 
</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A person
violating this chapter commits a traffic infraction and is subject to a
monetary penalty of forty-eight dollars.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 16,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;page-break-after:avoid'><a
name="_Toc519075540"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>14A.50         PARKING,
STANDING AND STOPPING</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.010   Tow-away
zones.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.020   Outside
allowed time periods.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.030   Angle
parking.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.040   Wide
commercial vehicles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.050   Trailers.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.060   Residential
mailboxes.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.070   Leaving
less than ten feet of roadway available for traffic.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.080   In
alley blocking driveway entrance.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.090   Passenger
loading zones.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.100   Buses,
taxicabs, for-hire vehicles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.110   Bus
stops, taxicab stands.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.120   Loading
zones.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.130   Advertising
and sales, washing, greasing, repairs.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.140   Special
terms or conditions of permits.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.150   One-way
roads.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.160   Blocking
access to vacant parking space.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.170   Bicycles.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.180   Monetary
penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.190   Failure
to respond to notice of traffic infraction – penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.010 
Tow-away zones.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to stop, stand, or park a vehicle in a place marked as a
tow-away zone during hours when the provisions applicable to such zone are in
effect.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 18,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.020  Outside
allowed time periods.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to park a vehicle upon any streets or parts of the streets
outside the allowed time period when signs are erected giving notice when
parking is allowed.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 19,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.030  Angle
parking.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to park a vehicle upon streets that have been marked or signed
for either back-in or front-in angle parking, at an angle in relation to the
curb or margin of the shoulder, other than is consistent with the markings or
signs.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 20,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.040  Wide
commercial vehicles.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to park a commercial vehicle that is more than eighty inches
wide overall on any county road or portion of county road between midnight and
6:00 a.m.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 21,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.050  Trailers.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except when necessary
to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at the
direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful for
any person to park a trailer, either attached to or detached from a motor
vehicle at any time, upon any county road or portion of the county road when
signs are erected giving notice that trailer parking is prohibited.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 22, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.060  Residential
mailboxes.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to park directly adjacent to a curbside, next to clearly visible
residential mailboxes between 9:00 a.m. and 9:00 p.m. on any day of scheduled
mail delivery by the United States Postal Service.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 23, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.070  Leaving
less than ten feet of roadway available for traffic.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except when necessary
to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at the
direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful for
any person to park a vehicle upon a county road in a manner or under conditions
that leave less than ten feet of the width of the roadway available for free
movement of vehicular traffic.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 24,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.080  In
alley blocking driveway entrance.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except when necessary
to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at the
direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful for
any person to stop, stand or park a vehicle within an alley in a position that
blocks the driveway entrance to any abutting property.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 25, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.090  Passenger
loading zones.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to stop, stand or park a vehicle for any purpose or period other
than for the expeditious loading or unloading of passengers in any place marked
as a passenger loading zone during hours when the provisions applicable to the
loading zone are effective, and then only for a maximum of three minutes.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 26, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.100 
Buses, taxicabs, for-hire vehicles.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A.  Except when
necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at
the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for an operator of a bus to stop, stand or park the bus upon any county road at
any place other than a designated bus stop.  This subsection does not prevent
the operator of a bus from temporarily stopping in accordance with other
stopping, standing or parking provisions at any place for the purpose of and
while actually engaged in the expeditious loading or unloading of passengers or
their baggage.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for the operator of a bus to enter a bus stop or passenger loading zone on a
county road in such a manner that, when stopped to load or unload passengers or
baggage, the right front wheel of the bus is more than eighteen inches from the
curb and the bus is not aligned parallel to the curb so as not to unduly impede
the movement of other vehicular traffic.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  Except when necessary to avoid
conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at the direction of a
deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful for the operator of a
taxicab or a vehicle for hire or transportation network company to stop, stand
or park the taxicab or vehicle for hire upon any county road at any place other
than in a designated taxicab stand.  This subsection does not prevent the
operator of a taxicab or vehicle for hire from temporarily stopping in
accordance with other stopping, standing or parking provisions at any place for
the purpose of and while actually engaged in the expeditious loading or
unloading of passengers.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 27,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.110  Bus
stops, taxicab stands.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except when necessary to avoid conflict with
traffic or in compliance with the law or at the direction of deputy or official
traffic control device, it is unlawful for any person to stop, stand or park a
vehicle in a bus stop or a taxicab stand, other than a bus in a bus stop or a
taxicab or vehicle for hire in a taxicab stand, when the stop or stand has been
designated and signed.  However, the driver of a passenger vehicle may
temporarily stop in a bus stop or a taxicab stand for the purpose of, or while
actually engaged in, loading or unloading passengers when the stopping does not
interfere with any bus, taxicab or vehicle for hire waiting to enter or about
to enter the stop or stand.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 28,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.120  Loading
zones.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to stop, stand, or park a vehicle for any purpose or period of
time other than for the expeditious unloading and delivery or pickup and
loading of property in any place marked as a loading zone during hours when the
provisions applicable to such zone are in effect. In no case shall the stop for
loading and unloading of property exceed thirty minutes.  The driver of a
vehicle may stop temporarily at a loading zone for the purpose of and while
actually engaged in loading or unloading passengers when such stopping does not
interfere with any vehicle which is waiting to enter or about to enter such
zone to load or unload property.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 29,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.130  Advertising
and sales, washing, greasing, repairs.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  No person
shall park any vehicle upon any county road for the principle purpose of:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>             1. 
Displaying advertising;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>             2. 
Displaying such vehicle for sale; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>             3. 
Selling merchandise from such vehicle, except when authorized.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  No person shall park any vehicle
upon any roadway for the principle purpose of washing, greasing, or repairing
such vehicle except repairs necessitated by an emergency.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 30, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.140  Special
terms or conditions of permits.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except when necessary
to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or at the
direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful for
any permittee or other person to violate any of the special terms or conditions
of any permit issued by the traffic engineer for the backing of a vehicle to
the curb for the purpose of loading or unloading property.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 31, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.150  One-way
roads.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Except
when necessary to avoid conflict with traffic or in compliance with the law or
at the direction of a deputy or official traffic control device, it is unlawful
for any person to stand or park a vehicle upon the left-hand side of such
one-way roadway unless signs are erected to permit such standing or parking
when a county road includes two or more separate roadways.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 32, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.160  Blocking
access to vacant parking space.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The driver of any
vehicle who first begins driving or maneuvering the driver's vehicle into a
vacant parking space shall have a prior right of way to park in the space, and
it shall be unlawful for another driver to attempt to deprive the driver of the
space by blocking the driver's access or otherwise.  For the purpose of
establishing right of way in this section it shall be considered proper to back
into any but a front-in angle parking space.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 33,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.170 
Bicycles.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>No
person shall park a bicycle upon a county road other than in the following
manner:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  At least
fifteen feet or as far as practicable from the edge of the roadway in areas
without sidewalk; or</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  Upon a
sidewalk but only if the sidewalk is equipped with a rack to support the
bicycle; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  In such manner as to afford the
least obstruction to pedestrian traffic.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 34,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.180 
Monetary penalties.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A
person violating this chapter commits a traffic infraction and is subject to
the base monetary penalty listed in the following table.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Section                                                 Base
Penalty</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.010:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.020:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.030:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.040:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.050:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.060:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.070:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.080:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.090:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.100:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.110:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.120:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.130:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.140:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.150:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.160:                               $20</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.50.170:                               $20.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 35, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.50.190  Failure
to respond to notice of traffic infraction – penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There shall be a
penalty of twenty-five dollars for failure to respond to a notice of traffic
infraction as listed in K.C.C. 4A.50.180.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 36,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;page-break-after:avoid'><a
name="_Toc519075541"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>14A.60         IMPOUNDMENT
OR SEIZURE</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.010   Impoundment
– vehicle of driver arrested for violation of RCW                                46.20.342
or 46.20.345.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.020   Impoundment
as provided by law – warrant might be required –                                   common
law, statute, ordinance may apply.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.030   Impoundment
of watercraft - exception - waiver.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.040   Impound
procedure.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.050   Owner
of impounded watercraft to be notified.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.060   Authorization
to impound form required.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.070   Administrative
hearing officers – conducting hearings required under                                       RCW
46.55.120(2) – request of hearing in accordance with RCW                                46.55.120(2).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.080   Redeeming
after impound – deadline – procedure if deemed                                                unclaimed
– notice – auction.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.090   Redeeming
impounded watercraft – requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.100   Record
of impounded vehicles or watercraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.110   Negotiation
and contracting for towing, storage and release of                                     impounded
vehicles and watercraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.120   Towing
contractor requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.130   Liability
for abandonment of vehicle or automobile hulk – relief upon                                   compliance
with RCW 46.12.650.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.140   Report
to Washington State Patrol of reported stolen or recovered                                    vehicles,
abandoned vehicles or automobile hulks – placing of                                   abandoned
vehicles or automobile hulks in custody of tow truck                                       operator.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.010  Impoundment
– vehicle of driver arrested for violation of RCW 6.20.342 or 46.20.345.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>As authorized in RCW
46.55.113, whenever the driver of a vehicle is arrested for violation of RCW
46.20.342 or 46.20.345, the vehicle is subject to summary impoundment, at the
discretion of the deputy, at the business location of a registered tow truck
operator approved by the sheriff.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 38,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.020  Impoundment
as provided by law – warrant might be required – common law, statute, ordinance
may apply.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A
vehicle may be impounded as provided by law.  This section shall not be
construed to authorize seizure of a vehicle without a warrant where a warrant
would otherwise be required.  This section shall not derogate from the powers
of the sheriff or deputies under the common law or other statute or ordinance.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 39, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.030  Impoundment
of watercraft - exception - waiver.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Whenever
it appears reasonably necessary to protect persons or property, the sheriff or a
deputy may order the impoundment of a watercraft when the watercraft cannot be
otherwise secured or released.  The sheriff or the deputy in lieu of impound
may release the watercraft to a person who, in the sheriff's or the deputy's
opinion, can safely operate the watercraft or secure the watercraft to a
moorage facility when the moorage facility has been approved for that purpose. 
A person to whom the sheriff or the deputy releases the watercraft must be
legally able operate a watercraft under RCW 79A.60.640.  If the owner or
operator of the watercraft is present, the person's signature on a waiver of
impound is required before the sheriff or the deputy may release the watercraft
to a person in lieu of impoundment.  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 41,
2018:  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 17668 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>
3, 2013.  Formerly K.C.C. 46.08.055).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.040  Impound
procedure.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>When the sheriff or the deputy orders an impoundment that
is authorized by this chapter, a towing contractor acting at the request of the
sheriff, the deputy or an authorized agent of the sheriff may impound the
vehicle or watercraft.  The sheriff, the deputy or the authorized agent must
provide to the towing contractor a signed authorization for the tow and the
impound before the towing contractor may proceed with the impound.  (Ord. 18743
</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 43, 2018:  Ord. 17668 </span><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>
4, 2013:  Ord. 10278 § 6, 1992</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.  Formerly K.C.C. 46.08.060).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.050  Owner
of impounded watercraft to be notified.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          A.  When a
watercraft is impounded, the impounding towing contractor shall notify the
legal and registered owner or owners of the impoundment of the watercraft.  The
notification shall be in writing and sent within twenty-four hours after the
impound by first-class mail to the last known registered and legal owner or
owners of the watercraft, as identified by the sheriff, and shall inform the
owner or owners of the identity of the person or agency authorizing the
impound. The notification shall include the name of the impounding tow firm,
its address and telephone number, the location and time of the impound and by
whose authority the watercraft was impounded.  The notice shall also include
the notice of the right of redemption and opportunity for a hearing to contest
the validity of the impoundment under K.C.C. 14A.60.070, as set forth on a form
to be provided by the [sheriff]<b>*</b>.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          B.  In the case
of an abandoned watercraft, within twenty-four hours after receiving
information on the watercraft owner or owners from the state Department of
Licensing, the towing contractor shall send by certified mail, with return
receipt requested, a notice of custody and sale to the legal and registered
owner or owners.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          C.  A notice
does not need be sent to the legal or registered owner or owners of an
impounded watercraft if the watercraft has been redeemed.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          D.  When a
person seeks to redeem an impounded watercraft, as provided for in this chapter
or by other law, the towing contractor shall give the person a copy of the towing
and storage receipt as well as written notice of the right of redemption and
opportunity for a hearing, as set forth on a form provided by the sheriff.  The
towing contractor shall maintain a record evidenced by the redeeming person's
signature that such notification was provided.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          E.  When the
sheriff authorizes the release of a watercraft that was impounded for
investigatory purposes, the towing contractor shall give the person a copy of
the towing and storage receipt as well as written notice of the right of
redemption and opportunity for a hearing, as set forth on a form provided by
the sheriff.  The towing contractor shall maintain a record evidenced by the
redeeming person's signature that such notification was provided.  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord.
18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 45, 2018:  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 17668 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>
5, 2013:  Ord. 10278 § 7, 1992.  Formerly K.C.C. 46.08.070).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Reviser's note:  Added
but not underlined in Ordinance 18743.  See K.C.C. 1.24.075.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.060  Authorization
to impound form required.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>All vehicles and watercraft impounded by the
sheriff shall utilize a written authorization to impound form, approved by the
sheriff.  The form shall denote the sheriff's authority to impound in chapter
46.55 RCW.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 46,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.070  Administrative
hearing officers – conducting hearings required under RCW 46.55.120(2) –
request of hearing in accordance with RCW 46.55.120(2).</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  In
accordance with RCW 46.55.240(1)(d), the sheriff shall appoint one or more
administrative hearing officers to conduct the hearings specified in and
requested under RCW 46.55.120(2).  Persons whose watercraft are impounded may
also request a hearing, which shall be carried out in accordance with the
processes for impound hearings specified in RCW 46.55.120(2).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  In accordance with RCW
46.55.240(1)(d), a decision made by an administrative hearing officer may be
appealed to the district court for final judgment.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 47, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.080  Redeeming
after impound – deadline – procedure if deemed unclaimed – notice – auction.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  An
impounded vehicle or watercraft not redeemed within fifteen days of mailing of
the notice required by RCW 46.55.110 or K.C.C. 14A.60.050, and not listed as
stolen, shall be deemed unclaimed and shall be sold at a public auction in
accordance with the provisions and subject to all conditions of RCW 46.55.130. 
When a timely request for a hearing has been made under RCW 46.55.120(2)(b),
the sale of the watercraft at public auction shall not take place until after
the hearing has been conducted and the hearing officer has entered an order. 
Before sale at public auction, the towing contractor shall confirm with the
sheriff that a hearing or hearing appeal, is not pending.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  When an
unclaimed watercraft is sold at public auction under subsection A. of this
section, the towing contractor may recover its towing and storage charges from
the proceeds of the sale.  The towing and storage charges shall be limited to
the contract rates established under K.C.C. 14A.60.110.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 48, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.090 
Redeeming impounded watercraft – requirements.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Watercraft impounded by
the county shall be redeemed under the following circumstances:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  Only
those persons authorized by RCW 46.55.120(1)(a) may redeem an impounded
watercraft.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  A person
redeeming an impounded watercraft must pay the towing contractor for the
reasonable costs of towing and storage resulting from the impoundment before
the watercraft may be released from impound.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 49,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.100 
Record of impounded vehicles or watercraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The sheriff shall keep
a record of all vehicles or watercraft impounded under chapter 46.55 RCW and
this chapter.  The record shall include at least the following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  Vehicle
or watercraft make, year and model;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  Vehicle
or watercraft license number and state of registration;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          C.  Vehicle
or watercraft identification number, if ascertainable;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          D.  Such
other descriptive information as the sheriff deems useful for purposes of
vehicle or watercraft identification;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          E.  Name of
impounding officer and serial number; and</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          F.  Reason for impoundment, and the
time, date and location the approved towing company took custody.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 50, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.110  Negotiation
and contracting for towing, storage and release of impounded vehicles and
watercraft.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The
sheriff shall negotiate and contract with one or more licensed and authorized
tow truck operators to tow, store and release vehicles and watercraft impounded
under this chapter or chapter 46.55 RCW.  At minimum, this contract for
services shall include a provision that indemnifies the county, and its
officials, from liability for any damages caused to the impounded vehicle or
watercraft during its tow or storage.  The contracts shall be at no cost to the
county and shall provide that the towing contractor may recover the costs of
towing and storage only from the person seeking to redeem the impounded vehicle
or watercraft, or from the proceeds of sale of an unclaimed vehicle or
watercraft as authorized by chapter 46.55 RCW or under K.C.C. 14A.60.070, and
that the county shall not be responsible for payment of the costs except upon
order of the administration hearing officer under K.C.C. 14A.60.070.  The
sheriff may specify that towing services shall be on a rotational or other
basis in specific geographic areas in the county.  The sheriff may specify the
rates towing contractors may charge persons seeking to redeem impounded
vehicles or watercraft for towing and storage services provided in accordance
with this chapter.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 51,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.120 
Towing contractor requirements.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Each towing contractor,
in addition to fully complying with the standards set by the sheriff, must:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          A.  File its
towing and storage rates with the sheriff;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  For impoundments authorized under
K.C.C. chapter 14A.60, maintain all vehicle and watercraft impound files for
three years.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 52,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.130 
Liability for abandonment of vehicle or automobile hulk – relief upon compliance
with RCW 46.12.650.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          </span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A.  The abandonment of
any vehicle or automobile hulk shall constitute a prima facie presumption that
the last owner of record is responsible for such abandonment and thus liable
for any costs incurred in removing, storing, and disposing of any abandoned
vehicle.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>          B.  A
registered owner transferring a vehicle shall be relieved from personal
liability under this section if the owner complies with the requirements of RCW
46.12.650.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 53,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.60.140  Report
to Washington State Patrol of reported stolen or recovered vehicles, abandoned
vehicles or automobile hulks – placing of abandoned vehicles or automobile
hulks in custody of tow truck operator.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>The sheriff shall
report to the chief of the Washington State Patrol all motor vehicles reported
to them as stolen or recovered, upon forms to be provided by the chief of the
Washington state patrol.  The sheriff shall report to the chief of the
Washington State Patrol all vehicles or automobile hulks found abandoned on a
county road or at any other place in the county and the vehicles or automobile
hulks shall, at the direction of a sheriff or deputy, be placed in the custody
of a tow truck operator registered under chapter 46.55 RCW.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 54, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;page-break-after:avoid'><a
name="_Toc519075542"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>14A.70         PROHIBITIONS
OF CERTAIN ACTIVITIES WITH VEHICLES, BICYCLES AND ANIMALS</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.010   Driving
across newly made pavement or freshly applied markings in                                 presence
of warning device.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.020   Boarding
or alighting moving vehicle prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.030   Monetary
penalties.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.040   Failure
to respond to notice of traffic infraction – penalty</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.010  Driving
across newly made pavement or freshly applied markings in presence of warning
device.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>No
person shall ride or drive any animal, bicycle, or vehicle, across any newly
made pavement or freshly applied markings on any county road when a sign, cone
marker, or other warning device is in place warning persons not to drive across
such pavement or marking.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 56,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.020  Boarding
or alighting moving vehicle prohibited.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>No person shall board
or alight from any vehicle while such vehicle is in motion.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 57, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.030 
Monetary penalties.</span></b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>A
person violating K.C.C. 14A.70.010 and 14A.70.020 commits a traffic infraction
and is subject to the base monetary penalty listed in the following table.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Section                                                 Base
Penalty</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.70.010:                                         $48</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;text-autospace:none'><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>K.C.C. 14A.70.020:                                         $48.</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 
(Ord. 18743 </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 58, 2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.70.040  Failure
to respond to notice of traffic infraction – penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There shall be a
penalty of twenty-five dollars for failure to respond to a notice of traffic
infraction as listed in K.C.C. 14A.70.030.</span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  (Ord. 18743 </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 59,
2018).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal align=center style='text-align:center;page-break-after:avoid'><a
name="_Toc519075543"><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>14A.80         VEHICULAR
TRESPASS</span></b></a></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.80.010   Avoidance
of stop signs and stop lights prohibited.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.80.020   Penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          <b>14A.80.010  Avoidance
of stop signs and stop lights prohibited.</b>  </span><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>No one driving a motor vehicle shall
seek to avoid stopping for stop signs, stop lights, yield signs or any other
sign or device used to control traffic using a public right-of-way by detouring
through private property to reach any other public or private right-of-way.  <span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>(Ord. 18743 </span></span><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 62,
2018:  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Ord.
10128 § 1, 1991.  Formerly K.C.C. 46.14.010).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><b><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>          14A.80.020  Penalty.</span></b><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  </span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Anyone found to be in
violation of the provisions of this chapter shall be guilty of an infraction
punishable by a fine of no more than twenty five dollars.  (<span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Ord. 18743 </span></span><span style='font-size:
12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>§</span><span
style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'> 62,
2018:  </span><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>Ord.
10128 § 2, 1991.  Formerly K.C.C. 46.14.020).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify'><span style='font-size:12.0pt;
font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

